Design for Recycling is a design strategy that incorporates recycling and recyclability criteria
into the design phase of products with the aim of obtaining recycled and/or recyclable products at the end of their useful life and returning them into the supply chain. When designing a product that should be recycled, it is useful to concentrate on the product rather than on the singular materials of the product. This because the design should consider the materials of a product together and how they will be managed in the system. 

This is the first strategy draft, you can help Circular Design by expanding it using the Contribute button on the Home page.